+# Reusable iOS custody acceptance fixture
+
+This overlay targets public commit `551576a03a4ef4f4b081e6191ce0a02c5947c679`
+and product patch SHA-256
+`d2c7e8c94adc37343c21324173b96e9b3675a9c7f1a5b0ffda08db1293081bef`.
+Apply the fixture overlay to a dedicated checkout at that commit. Pass the
+product patch separately. The runner verifies the public tree and the patch's
+five preimages and postimages before applying fixture-only changes to its
+disposable source copy.
+
+```sh
+base=551576a03a4ef4f4b081e6191ce0a02c5947c679
+# Set native_checkout to a fresh path and fixture_overlay to the delivered patch.
+git --no-replace-objects worktree add --detach "$native_checkout" "$base"
+cd "$native_checkout"
+git apply --check "$fixture_overlay"
+git apply "$fixture_overlay"
+
+product_patch=/Users/andreyyurlov/.t3/worktrees/mixer/t3-e555d928/verification/local/l07-ios-supervisor-compat/l07-ios-worker-reusable-supervisor-compat-1e2de013.patch
+mkdir -p verification/local
+fixture=tests/integration/l07-ios-active-custody
+python3 -B -W error::SyntaxWarning -W error::ResourceWarning -m unittest discover \
+  -s "$fixture" -p test_reusable.py -v
+python3 -B "$fixture/reusable.py" --check-fixture --product-patch "$product_patch" \
+  --receipt verification/local/l07-reusable-fixture-check.json
+```
+
+The fixture check verifies the exact product patch and parses the composed
+Elixir sources. It starts no listener, compiler, database, or device.
+
+## Admit a pinned Starter stage
+
+Use the original fixture's pinned arm64 Mach-O CLI and iOS Starter export.
+Reuse a positively closed stage if its exact receipt, CLI, and export are
+available. For a fresh stage, the checkout needs these Git objects:
+
+- Restore launcher `57f3ed4f17b80f15fc6d646b14c6dbfa05bd7eea`
+- Starter CLI `201ead70ff68bfe18de24c0642f518701459e0a4`
+- Starter SDK `fad0d0b3e65fd3be3b49675601693e5d91999fbe`
+
+The fresh stage builds Swift dependencies and exports Starter. It does not run
+a fixture build POST or a Starter Xcode build.
+
+```sh
+python3 -B tests/integration/hosted-expiry-restore/replay-starter.py --stage-only
+# Set stage_receipt to the absolute result.json path printed after PASS_STAGE.
+stage_dir="${stage_receipt%/*}"
+stage_sha256="$(shasum -a 256 < "$stage_receipt" | cut -d ' ' -f 1)"
+starter_cli="$(python3 -B -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))["commands"]["starter-export"]["argv"][0])' "$stage_receipt")"
+
+python3 -B "$fixture/reusable.py" --preflight-only --product-patch "$product_patch" \
+  --stage-receipt "$stage_receipt" --stage-sha256 "$stage_sha256" \
+  --cli "$starter_cli" --export "$stage_dir/starter/exported" \
+  --receipt verification/local/l07-reusable-starter-preflight.json
+```
+
+## Run the live acceptance
+
+Use macOS arm64, Python 3.14, the selected Xcode 27.2 build 27B52, PostgreSQL
+17, Elixir 1.20.4 on OTP 29, and Hex 2.5.1 with the 21 locked dependency archives
+and registry prewarmed. Override the defaults with `--pg-bin`, `--hex-cache`,
+and `--mix-archives` when needed. Scratch needs a canonical path with trusted
+ancestors. Both builds target the generic iOS Simulator SDK with signing
+disabled. They require no booted device.
+
+```sh
+python3 -B "$fixture/reusable.py" --live --product-patch "$product_patch" \
+  --stage-receipt "$stage_receipt" --stage-sha256 "$stage_sha256" \
+  --cli "$starter_cli" --export "$stage_dir/starter/exported" \
+  --receipt verification/local/l07-reusable-live.json
+```
+
+The runner starts an isolated SCRAM PostgreSQL 17 cluster and the stock
+restricted Phoenix API and Oban processor under fixture-specific credentials.
+The fixture seeds one scoped Starter input to exercise build creation and
+custody. It issues two signed-in create requests with distinct idempotency
+keys. Both operations use one registration, one read-only configuration, one
+ledger and authority, one loopback listener address, and the same independent
+supervisor. The fixture pauses between operations to verify each build's
+binding before dispatch.
+
+The runner requires a live owned Xcode receipt and exact process identities
+before it kills the original listener PID. It immediately rebinds the same
+loopback port via the documented worker entry point. It requires inclusive
+receipt timing around the signal, the original supervisor's terminal CLI proof,
+the exact Swift and Xcode receipts, and A's later Oban guard and one terminal
+journal entry and capacity release. It then verifies three authenticated
+downloads and authenticated logs for both A and B, and rechecks A's SQLite row,
+claim, journal, and download hashes after B.
+
+Each scenario allows 45 seconds for a witnessed Xcode launch, 430 seconds for
+terminal native custody, and 30 seconds for settlement. A run can fail if it
+misses the Xcode RUNNING receipt, the port cannot rebind within eight seconds,
+or archived artifacts exceed the existing fixture's 128 MiB download limit.
+Only A's listener is interrupted. A missing acknowledgment or another
+unverified terminal chain leaves native custody unresolved. Preserve the
+reported private scratch and command identities on exit 74. Never retry or
+operate on that chain based on the listener or supervisor's direct exit. For a
+closed failure, the runner reports private service diagnostics and port-reuse
+observations. A successful run checks port reuse and removes its live scratch.
+The operator owns the dedicated checkout and any separately prepared stage.
